nt"}],"gloss":"thus"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சொல்லவும்","parts":[{"text":"சொல்","lemma":"col","gloss":"to say"},{"text":"அவும்","lemma":"avum","gloss":"even though"}],"gloss":"even though told"},{"surface":"தேறீர்","parts":[{"text":"தேறு","lemma":"tēṟu","gloss":"to understand"},{"text":"ஈர்","lemma":"īr","gloss":"you plural"}],"gloss":"you do not understand"},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if so"}],"gloss":"if so"},{"surface":"மெல்லியல்","parts":[{"text":"மெல்","lemma":"mel","gloss":"soft"},{"text":"இயல்","lemma":"iyal","gloss":"nature"}],"gloss":"soft-natured"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கழற்","parts":[{"text":"கழற்","lemma":"கழற்","gloss":"molucca bean"}],"gloss":"molucca bean","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கனி","parts":[{"text":"கனி","lemma":"kaṉi","gloss":"fruit"}],"gloss":"fruit"},{"surface":"வகுத்த","parts":[{"text":"வகு","lemma":"vaku","gloss":"to divide"},{"text":"த்த","lemma":"tta","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"divided"},{"surface":"துணைச்","parts":[{"text":"துணை","lemma":"tuṇai","gloss":"double/match"},{"text":"ச்","lemma":"c","gloss":"sandhi consonant"}],"gloss":"matching"},{"surface":"சில்","parts":[{"text":"சில்","lemma":"cil","gloss":"few"}],"gloss":"few"},{"surface":"ஓதிக்","parts":[{"text":"ஓதி","lemma":"ōti","gloss":"hair"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"sandhi consonant"}],"gloss":"hair"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குறுந்தொடி","parts":[{"text":"குறும்","lemma":"kuṟum","gloss":"small"},{"text":"தொடி","lemma":"toṭi","gloss":"bangles"}],"gloss":"small bangles"},{"surface":"மகளிர்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"women"}],"gloss":"women"},{"surface":"தோள்விடல்","parts":[{"text":"தோள்","lemma":"tōḷ","gloss":"shoulders"},{"text":"விடல்","lemma":"viṭal","gloss":"leaving"}],"gloss":"leaving the shoulders"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இறும்பூது","parts":[{"text":"இறும்பூது","lemma":"iṟumpūtu","gloss":"wonder"}],"gloss":"wonder"},{"surface":"அன்று","parts":[{"text":"அன்று","lemma":"aṉṟu","gloss":"it is not"}],"gloss":"it is not"},{"surface":"அஃது","parts":[{"text":"அஃது","lemma":"அஃது","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அறிந்து","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"aṟi","gloss":"to know"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having known"},{"surface":"ஆடுமினே","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"āṭu","gloss":"to act/play"},{"text":"மின்","lemma":"miṉ","gloss":"imperative plural suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"clitic"}],"gloss":"act accordingly!"}]}],"literal":"Swords, rubbed and sharpened for war, rejoicing, / because of destroying the protected fortress walls of those who opposed, / plunged so that flesh touched, and lost their form. / Spears, having crossed the fortresses of those who held small forts, / because of ruining the country of fragrant toddy, / with dark shafts clasped by ferrules, / their joints shaken, changed their position. / Elephants, fighting the doors that bore the wooden bolts, / because of breaking the strongholds of their herds of elephants, / their thick-bound tusk-rings slipped off. / Horses, of the warriors who fought together spreading out, / because of galloping so that golden beautiful garlands perished, / struggling on the battlefield and becoming weary, have distressed hooves. / He himself, with an ocean-like army that shakes the earth, / wearing golden tumba flowers and heroic anklets, / has a circular shield with holes struck by arrows. / In that place, how can those who opposed escape? If you want / the ancient town of abundance with paddy of tightly packed ears / to belong to you, you must pay tribute to him who approached. If you refuse, / he is not one to agree, he of winning wars, thus / even if told, if you do not understand, / abandoning the shoulders of women with small bangles / and few locks of hair parted like split molucca beans / is not a wonder. Know that and act!","translation":"The swords, sharpened for battle, have lost their shape from plunging deep into the flesh of enemies while destroying their guarded fortresses. The spears, having breached the strongholds of rebel chiefs and ruined their lands rich in fragrant toddy, have shaken joints and bent shafts. The war elephants, battering doors secured with heavy wooden bolts and crushing enemy herds, have lost the thick bands on their tusks. The horses of the warriors who charged in unison, galloping hard and trampling golden garlands, have worn and battered hooves from struggling on the battlefield. As for the king himself, whose army is like a land-shaking ocean, his circular shield is riddled with holes from arrows met in battle. How then can his enemies survive? If you wish to retain your ancient, fertile towns rich in dense ears of paddy, you must go to him and pay tribute. If you refuse, he is not one to relent, for he is a victor in war. If you do not understand this even when told, then having to abandon the soft shoulders of your women, whose sparse hair is parted like split molucca beans and who wear small bangles, will be no surprise. Know this, and act accordingly!","modern":"போருக்காகத் தீட்டப்பட்டு, பகைவரின் அரண்களை அழித்ததால், சதையில் மூழ்கித் தங்கள் வடிவத்தை இழந்தன வாள்கள். குறுநில மன்னர்களின் கோட்டைகளை வென்று, நறுமணமுள்ள கள் நிறைந்த நாட்டை அழித்ததால், பூண்களால் கட்டப்பட்ட ஈட்டிகளின் காம்புகள் நிலை குலைந்து போயின. பெரிய மரத்தாழ்ப்பாள்களைத் தாங்கிய கதவுகளை முட்டி மோதி, பகைவரின் யானைப்படைகளை அழித்ததால், போர்க்களத்து யானைகளின் தந்த வளையங்கள் கழன்று விழுந்தன. பரவி நின்று போரிட்ட வீரர்களின் குதிரைகள், பொன் மாலைகள் அழியும்படி ஓடி, போர்க்களத்தில் உழன்று களைப்படைந்ததால், அவற்றின் குளம்புகள் சிதைந்து போயின. அவனோ, நிலத்தை அதிரச் செய்யும் கடல் போன்ற படையைக் கொண்டவன்; பொன் தும்பை மாலையும் வீரக்கழலும் அணிந்தவன்; அவனது வட்டக் கேடயம் அம்புகள் பாய்ந்து துளைகளுடன் காணப்படுகிறது. அப்படியிருக்க, அவனுடன் போரிட்ட பகைவர்கள் தப்பிப்பது எப்படி? நெற்கதிர்கள் நிறைந்த உங்களுடைய பழமையான ஊர்கள் உங்களுக்கே சொந்தமாக இருக்க வேண்டுமானால், அவனிடம் சென்று திறை செலுத்த வேண்டும். மறுத்தால், அவன் சமாதானம் ஆகமாட்டான்; அவன் போரில் வெல்பவன். இதைச் சொல்லியும் நீங்கள் உணராவிட்டால், பிளந்த கழற்சிக்காய் போன்ற கூந்தலையும் சிறிய வளையல்களையும் உடைய உங்கள் பெண்களின் தோள்களை நீங்கள் பிரிய நேரிடும். இதில் வியப்பொன்றும் இல்லை; இதனை அறிந்து செயல்படுங்கள்!","explanation":"This poem is in the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai (praising a king's greatness) and Iyaṉmoḻi tuṟai (advising others on how to act based on the king's nature), composed by the famous poet Avvaiyār in praise of Atiyamāṉ Neṭumāṉ Añci. The poet describes the devastating power of Atiyamāṉ's army by detailing the worn-out state of his weapons and animals: his swords are misshapen from cutting flesh, his spears are bent, his elephants' tusk-rings have slipped off from battering fort gates, and his horses' hooves are battered. Atiyamāṉ himself bears a shield riddled with arrow holes, showing his active participation in battle. Avvaiyār warns the opposing kings that if they wish to save their fertile lands, they must surrender and pay tribute. If they refuse, they will inevitably lose their kingdoms and be separated from their beloved wives, which would be no surprise given Atiyamāṉ's relentless nature in war.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.78],[0.9,1.4],[1.4,1.4],[1.4,1.8],[1.99,3.1],[3.1,3.5],[3.5,3.6],[3.6,3.9],[3.9,3.9],[3.9,5.4],[5.4,5.87],[5.87,5.98],[5.98,6.04],[6.04,7.7],[7.7,8.0],[8.0,8.4],[8.4,9.2],[9.2,10.2],[10.2,10.2],[10.2,10.2],[10.2,10.2],[10.2,10.2],[10.2,10.2],[10.2,12.3],[12.3,12.8],[12.8,12.9],[12.9,13.8],[13.8,14.2],[14.2,14.2],[14.2,14.2],[14.2,15.9],[15.9,16.1],[16.1,16.3],[16.3,16.7],[17.72,18.42],[18.42,18.52],[18.52,18.92],[18.92,19.34],[19.34,19.47],[19.47,19.47],[19.47,19.68],[19.68,21.76],[21.76,21.82],[21.82,23.02],[23.02,23.62],[23.62,23.72],[23.72,24.82],[24.82,24.92],[24.92,25.32],[25.32,26.15],[26.15,26.15],[26.15,26.15],[26.15,26.15],[26.15,26.15],[26.15,28.62],[28.62,29.52],[29.52,29.82],[29.82,29.92],[29.92,30.22],[3